    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS** with the full suite (3/3 tests green, including the three new postcode acceptance tests).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional, region-validated `postcode` on the create-owner endpoint, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema (`pattern: ^[0-9]{4}$`, not in `required`). The OpenAPI generator regenerates `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` with `getPostcode()`, and MapStruct maps it by name automatically (verified in the generated `OwnerMapperImpl`).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `postcode` field, `@Column`, and accessors so it persists and returns.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `postcode VARCHAR(9)` column to all four `schema.sql` variants (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres), and fixed the hsqldb `data.sql` positional seed inserts (the test profile is `hsqldb`) to include the extra column.\n\n4. **`RequirePostcode.java`** (new pipeline step) \u2014 validates the postcode **only when present**: rejects a non-4-digit value, then looks up the city's region via the existing `Locality` table and rejects a value outside that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). An unknown-region city accepts any 4-digit code; an absent postcode is skipped, keeping the request contract backward-compatible.\n\n5. **`InvalidPostcodeException` + handler + escalation YAML** \u2014 a checked exception that responds `400` with `{\"errors\":[\"postcode\"]}`, mirroring the existing `InvalidTelephoneException` pattern.\n\n6. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `requirePostcode` into the pipeline (after address normalization, before the transactional capacity checks), consistent with the other non-transactional validation steps.\n\nI scoped this to the create endpoint (`POST /api/owners`), which is where the spec and tests exercise postcode; the PUT path already ignores unmapped fields, so it stays unaffected and backward-compatible.",
